\DOC the_coinductive_definitions

\TYPE {the_coinductive_definitions : (thm * thm * thm) list ref}

\SYNOPSIS
List of all coinductive definitions introduced so far.

\DESCRIBE
The reference variable {the_coinductive_definitions} holds the list of
coinductive definitions made so far using {new_coinductive_definition}, which
automatically augments it.

\FAILURE
Not applicable.

\EXAMPLE
In HOL Light's initial state, no coinductive definitions have been made, and
after one has been, it appears in the list:
{
  # !the_coinductive_definitions;;
  val it : (thm * thm * thm) list = []
  # let infpath_RULES,infpath_COINDUCT,infpath_CASES =
      new_coinductive_definition
       `!x:A y. R x y /\ infpath R y ==> infpath R x`;;
  ...
  # !the_coinductive_definitions;;
  val it : (thm * thm * thm) list =
    [(|- !R x y. R x y /\ infpath R y ==> infpath R x,
      |- !R infpath'.
             (!a. infpath' a ==> (?y. R a y /\ infpath' y))
             ==> (!a. infpath' a ==> infpath R a),
      |- !R a. infpath R a <=> (?y. R a y /\ infpath R y))]
}

\USES
This list is not logically necessary and is not part of HOL Light's logical
core, but it is used outside the core so that multiple instances of the same
coinductive definition are quietly ``ignored'' rather than rejected.
Users may also sometimes find it convenient.

\SEEALSO
new_coinductive_definition, the_inductive_definitions.

\ENDDOC
